This is important enough that I want to formally record it.

Decision: Every gateway returns exactly one canonical protocol artifact.

Gateway	Output
Intake	ClassificationResult
Static	StaticAnalysisResult
Dynamic (future)	BehaviorTranscript
Consensus (future)	VerificationSeal
Orchestrator	VerificationResult

This means gateways never inspect each other's internals. They communicate only through their protocol artifacts. That gives us loose coupling, clear interfaces, and makes each gateway independently testable.